physical_map.json PROVENANCE -- WHY THE BRIDGE SCRIPT WAS *NOT* RE-RUN
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Shipping route-optimizer's own shortening/physical_map.json, which was built FROM
  THE FINAL geometry.

  physical_map_from_placement.py was deliberately NOT re-run. That bridge reads the
  canonical layout/routes.json, which still holds the PRE-shortening routing, so it
  would have emitted a map describing wiring that no longer exists -- the stale-map
  failure mode, which is worse than a missing map because nothing downstream can
  detect it. There is no post-shortening routes.json to promote: route-optimizer
  emits an updated physical_map.json directly, not a routes.json.

  NON-DEGENERACY ASSERTED (independently, not trusted):
    devices with real positions : 11 / 11
    devices with rotation_deg   : 11 / 11
    devices with primitive_cell : 11 / 11
    nets traced                 : 10 / 10, all "source": "router"  (0 "unmatched")
    vias recorded               : 23  (matches the GDS/summary)
    Vin and Vip carry 0 segments by design -- they are 0-terminal external pins that
    land directly on device gates with no routed metal, identical to pass 1.

  MAP-vs-GDS METAL CHECK (this agent's own boolean test, not verify_shortening.py):
    153 map segments, total area 125.16 um^2, checked by gdstk boolean against the
    shipped GDS metal on the SAME layer:
      uncovered = 0.608 um^2 = 0.486%.  The residual is a 2 nm (0.002 um) sliver
      along segment edges -- the documented lambda-grid snap, not missing metal.
    CONTROL: the identical map against the PRE-shortening GDS is 29.01% uncovered.
    A 0.49% vs 29% split proves the shipped map describes the shipped geometry.

